== Mock Examination 1 — Questions

#mcq(1, [An alloy of tin and lead is used as], [brass], [bronze], [steel], [solder])

#mcq(2, [The mass of barium sulphate formed when excess barium chloride is added to 0.10 mol of sodium sulphate is], [11.7 g], [46.6 g], [23.3 g], [233 g])

#mcq(3, [The off-gas leaving the top of the blast furnace contains mainly], [oxygen and hydrogen], [nitrogen and carbon dioxide], [chlorine and hydrogen chloride], [sulphur dioxide])

#mcq(4, [Which of these is NOT a use of hydrogen?], [bleaching paper], [the Haber process], [hydrogenation of oils], [fuel cells])

#mcq(5, [Although a low temperature increases the yield of sulphur(VI) oxide, the industrial temperature is about 450 °C because], [the catalyst melts], [SO₃ decomposes], [the pressure is too high], [the reaction is too slow at low temperature])

#mcq(6, [The chief fuel of a cement kiln may be], [petrol], [natural gas or coal], [kerosene only], [wood])

#mcq(7, [The thermite reaction is], [endothermic and slow], [a neutralisation], [highly exothermic and used for welding], [a precipitation])

#mcq(8, [If 0.10 mol of calcium reacts completely with water, the volume of hydrogen at s.t.p. is], [2.24 dm³], [1.12 dm³], [4.48 dm³], [22.4 dm³])

#mcq(9, [The reaction Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂ is an example of], [oxidation of iron], [neutralisation], [displacement of iron by carbon], [reduction of iron ore])

#mcq(10, [Which statement about the Haber process is correct?], [it is endothermic and favoured by low pressure], [it is exothermic and favoured by high pressure], [it is exothermic and favoured by low pressure], [it is endothermic and favoured by high pressure])

#mcq(11, [The smell of a burning match comes from], [ozone], [chlorine], [sulphur(IV) oxide], [ammonia])

#mcq(12, [A green colour in ordinary glass usually comes from], [iron(II) compounds], [cobalt compounds], [copper(II) compounds], [manganese compounds])

#mcq(13, [A mineral from which a metal can be extracted profitably is called], [gangue], [a slag], [an alloy], [an ore])

#mcq(14, [Which property of the alkali metals makes them unsuitable for structural use?], [their high reactivity and softness], [their high density], [their high melting point], [their colour])

#mcq(15, [Which statement about aluminium and iron is correct?], [both are extracted by electrolysis], [iron is extracted by reduction with carbon monoxide and aluminium by electrolysis], [both are extracted by reduction with coke], [neither is extracted from an oxide])

#mcq(16, [Which of the following gases is collected over water?], [ammonia], [carbon dioxide], [hydrogen], [sulphur dioxide])

#mcq(17, [Oleum is], [a dilute solution of sulphuric acid], [sulphur(VI) oxide dissolved in concentrated sulphuric acid], [sulphur dissolved in water], [sodium sulphate solution])

#mcq(18, [Lead pollution of the air was reduced by], [replacing leaded petrol with unleaded petrol], [adding lead to diesel], [using taller chimneys], [burning more coal])

#mcq(19, [Which of the following is a use of copper that depends on its low reactivity?], [electrical wiring], [galvanising], [water pipes], [making steel])

#mcq(20, [Which observation shows that calcium is more reactive than magnesium?], [calcium is denser], [calcium is harder], [calcium has a higher melting point], [calcium reacts steadily with cold water while magnesium does not])

#mcq(21, [Slag floats on the molten iron because], [it is less dense], [it is denser], [it is a gas], [it is magnetic])

#mcq(22, [In the Haber process, the ammonia formed is removed by], [filtration], [cooling and liquefaction], [adding acid], [burning it])

#mcq(23, [0.20 mol of chlorine has a mass of], [7.1 g], [3.55 g], [14.2 g], [35.5 g])

#mcq(24, [The best way to deal with the large volume of household waste in a city is to], [burn everything in the open], [dump it in a river], [bury it in the garden], [reduce, reuse and recycle before disposal])

#mcq(25, [Which of these alloys contains no iron?], [stainless steel], [mild steel], [brass], [carbon steel])

#mcq(26, [A white solid dissolves in water to give a solution that turns red litmus blue. The solid could be], [sodium chloride], [copper(II) sulphate], [barium sulphate], [calcium oxide])

#mcq(27, [The white flame of burning magnesium is a use of magnesium in], [flares and fireworks], [aircraft alloys], [fertilisers], [batteries only])

#mcq(28, [Which of these gases is the main cause of the greenhouse effect from burning fossil fuels?], [nitrogen], [carbon dioxide], [oxygen], [argon])

#mcq(29, [Bleaching powder smells of chlorine because it], [contains free chlorine gas], [is prepared from chlorine], [reacts with carbon dioxide in the air to release chlorine], [reacts with water only])

#mcq(30, [Which of these is an air pollutant from the burning of sulphur-containing fuel?], [sulphur(IV) oxide], [nitrogen], [argon], [water vapour])

#mcq(31, [Which reaction would NOT occur?], [Zn + CuSO₄], [Fe + CuSO₄], [Mg + ZnSO₄], [Cu + ZnSO₄])

#mcq(32, [Which compound is used as a whitewash and in water treatment?], [sodium chloride], [calcium hydroxide], [barium sulphate], [magnesium sulphate])

#mcq(33, [The mass of aluminium in 204 g of pure alumina is], [108 g], [54 g], [162 g], [204 g])

#mcq(34, [Nitrogen fertilisers help plants because plants need nitrogen to make], [carbohydrates], [water], [proteins and nucleic acids], [cellulose only])

#mcq(35, [In the Contact process, the sulphur dioxide is purified and dried before it reaches the catalyst because], [the gas would explode], [the catalyst would melt], [sulphur would crystallise], [impurities poison the catalyst])

#mcq(36, [Which of these waters is the softest?], [water from a limestone cave], [rainwater], [sea water], [borehole water in a gypsum area])

#mcq(37, [0.20 mol of zinc displaces 0.20 mol of copper. The mass of copper deposited is], [6.4 g], [32 g], [64 g], [12.8 g])

#mcq(38, [Barium chloride is used in the laboratory to test for], [chloride ions], [sulphate ions], [carbonate ions], [nitrate ions])

#mcq(39, [The electrodes in the Hall–Héroult cell are made of], [carbon], [copper], [platinum], [steel])

#mcq(40, [Which conditions give the highest equilibrium yield of ammonia?], [high temperature and low pressure], [high temperature and high pressure], [low temperature and high pressure], [low temperature and low pressure])

